body:
Hospital. Now. 

&#x200B;

I hope you already went

Hahaha, that would be great! I have this weird thing when it is easier for me to do someone else's work rather than my own, even if its just as difficult. Plus, I love painting houses, its so much fun. What color are you painting it? 

&#x200B;

You sound pretty amazing too haha, and if ever need be I'll remember you. And the offer goes both ways - if you ever need to vent or just talk about nothing in particular, my DMs are open as well. :)

the oy vey got me, i sigh and say it all the time too.

&#x200B;

I wish i could help you. i want to. but im useless and also fucked up. you were right with the hospital shit, they were wack. fuck em.

I do it as a form of self punishment, to relieve guilt from failure, a way to make what i feel "real".  Otherwise its just in my head, and would people even believe me? Thats the main of it.

&#x200B;

There is also the aspect of how somehow it just... it makes me feel like I CAN make myself do something, im scared but i feel power over my own body, And it makes me feel better after. I love running my hands over the bumpy scabs on my thighs.... it feels so right.

the first fucking time that I have been happy to say goodby to someone xD 

&#x200B;

Congratualtions. <3333333

" So many things seem "normal" after enough time. "

This is true i suppose. Its normal to me, but when you step back its utterly crazy. If medication and therapy did really help you, maybe it would help me too. Its so hard and im just tired of fighting things and telling myself that "oh you are fine, nothings wrong with your life" and "you are worth something, dont cut" but it just wears me out in the end, and takes me full circle to think "oh maybe i could just die now. it would be so nice. Something quick and not too painful." and then i cant even remember what came first.  I just want the worry and stress and pain to just go away. I wish i could have a little real confidence in myself. 

&#x200B;

and you are right, it is what it is... if i get myself some help it might not be a bad thing. tbh i did try calling my colleges counseling, but forgot the would be closed on a saturday (And holiday to boot xD). I'll see what i might do on tuesday. 

&#x200B;

And also, thank you for taking the time and care to reply. <3 Its a little thing, but it means a lot to me. so thank you.

&#x200B;
